T-Time
======

Third-party material and how it is used. Licence verification status is stated
honestly; "unverified" means not yet checked.

- pyewts 1.0.0 (Apache-2.0): the inventory of standard implicit stacks in
  `STANDARD_STACKS` (crates/ttime-core/src/ewts/mod.rs) was derived in part from
  its published list, cross-checked against m17n behaviour. Also used as a
  differential oracle (not shipped).
- ewts-rs / crate `ewts` 0.1.4 (MIT OR Apache-2.0): differential oracle
  (`scripts/differential/ewts-rs-diff`, not shipped); the 16 inputs and expected
  outputs in `crates/ttime-core/tests/fixtures/thl_rules.tsv` come from its
  `rules_test.rs`, which transcribes THL rule examples.
- Keyman `tibetan_ewts` keyboard (MIT): behavioural reference and differential
  testing only; no rules copied.
- m17n-db `bo-ewts.mim` (LGPL 2.1+): behavioural reference only; no tables or
  text copied. Stack inventory agreement was checked by behaviour, not by copying.
- Botok, Tibetan NLP, TiSpell, OpenPecha, BDRC: unverified; unused.

Repository licence: undecided (MIT or Apache-2.0). Add LICENSE before release.
